 "Build a 4/4 build-up before a drop. Structure: 8 bars (16 bars for drum and bass). Seven bars of risers, drums and sustained instruments; the final bar is the pre-drop where everything else cuts off (snare roll, pre-drop vocal, sub build). Transitions: into the build-up use quiet up-risers and down-filters starting at its first bar; take one note of a chord-progression pad, hold it for the build, and automate pitch up over the last four bars; use vocals that actually say something in the last four bars (chop only the first four); thin the drums before the build if there is no breakdown, filter them in gradually if there is. Into the drop: always include one pre-drop bar, gradually automate low end out of bass, pads and risers, and optionally dip the loudest elements (not vocals) just before the drop. Elements: kick every beat for 4 bars, doubled for 2, doubled again for 1 (and through the last bar if the vocal matches), filtering out as it goes; a snare every step, filtering in from already half-open, plus a second low snare after 4 bars; hats/claps/percussion loop for depth; bring back an element from the intro/breakdown as a sustained part with a riser; layer multiple quiet risers.",
